// Exists for the EDITOR, not for any build or script.
//
// The test tree is type-checked by `../tsconfig.test.json` (the
// `typecheck:test` task), but an editor only auto-discovers `tsconfig.json` —
// and this package's includes `src` alone. Without this file the tests belong to
// no discoverable project, so the TS server falls back to an inferred project
// that loads every `@types` package in the tree: `@types/mocha` and
// `@types/jest` then both declare `describe` / `it` / `beforeEach`, and every
// test file shows `TS2403` clashes that no `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` run
// reproduces.
//
// Nothing else reads it: `typecheck:test` names its project explicitly, and
// vitest transpiles without type-checking. The base config's relative `include`
// stays correct here, because TypeScript resolves it against the file it
// originates in rather than the one that extends it.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.test.json"
}
